      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Torres Tejerizo et al.",
        "AbstractText": "Rhizobium tibeticum was originally isolated from root nodules of Trigonella archiducis-nicolai grown in Tibet, China. This species is also able to nodulate Medicago sativa and Phaseolus vulgaris The whole-genome sequence of the type strain, R. tibeticum CCBAU85039T, is reported in this study."
